
JPMS
  Java Platform Mudule System

  Accessibility in Java 1-8
    public
    protected
    package
    private

  Accessibility in Java 9+
    public to everyone
          // module-info.java
          module greetings {
              exports com.example.greetings;
          }
    public to friend modules
          exports com.example.greetings to app.module;
    public only within a module
          module internal.module {
            // No exports
          }
    protected
      Accessible within the same package and 
      if exported, then accessible in subclasses in other module.
    package-private(default)
    private





Key Keywords
  exports -Makes a package accessible to other modules
  requires -Declares dependency on another module
  opens- Allows reflective access (e.g., for frameworks like Spring or JAXB)
  uses/provides -Enables service loading via ServiceLoader
  requires transitive -Re-exports a dependency to downstream modules




